# deps / build
node_modules/
dist/
target/
build/
.dart_tool/
*.g.dart

# WP-R2-4: the bundled sidecar server payload is a BUILD ARTIFACT (rebuilt by
# apps/desktop/scripts/build-sidecar.mjs → `pnpm --filter @flowmic/desktop build:sidecar`).
# The build script is tracked; the emitted bundle is not.
apps/desktop/src-tauri/resources/server.js
# Emitted next to it by the same script: `{"type":"module"}`, which is what makes
# an older host Node read that ESM bundle as ESM instead of CJS (see the comment
# on OUT_PKG in build-sidecar.mjs). Same reason it is not tracked: it is emitted,
# not authored.
apps/desktop/src-tauri/resources/package.json
# The private Node runtime staged by the same script (owner 2026-08-03: the MSI
# ships one too, not just the portable bundle). ~83 MB of somebody else's release
# binary — copied at build time from the Node running the build, never tracked.
#
# 🔴 W3 2026-08-07 — the line below used to be the ONLY entry, and「never tracked」
# had quietly become false. MAC-03 made the staged filename per-platform, so on
# darwin the file is `resources/node` with no extension: `git check-ignore` exited
# 1 (NOT ignored) for a **112,915,776-byte** Mach-O. One `git add -A` on any macOS
# clone would have committed 113 MB of somebody else's release binary into a repo
# that is scheduled to go PUBLIC at 0.3.0 — and a large binary is not undone by a
# later `git rm`, it stays in history forever.
# ⇒ Matched by BASENAME so it cannot rot again the next time the name moves: the
# staged runtime is `resources/node` on darwin/linux and `resources/node.exe` on
# Windows, and both are emitted by build-sidecar.mjs from the pin in
# scripts/vendor/bundled-node.mjs. Nothing authored lives at either path.
apps/desktop/src-tauri/resources/node
apps/desktop/src-tauri/resources/node.exe
# ENG-1 / fix-028: the sherpa-onnx addon staged beside the bundle by the same
# script (stageSherpaAddon) — ~22 MB of somebody else's release binaries per
# platform (onnxruntime.dll, sherpa-onnx-c-api.dll, sherpa-onnx.node).
#
# The blanket `node_modules/` at the top of this file ALREADY matches it. This
# entry is written out anyway, for the reason the W3 block above this one was:
# the last time a large staged binary depended on an implicit rule, a rename
# (`node.exe` → `node` on darwin) silently moved it OUT of the ignore and put a
# 113 MB Mach-O one `git add -A` away from a repo scheduled to go public. An
# explicit, named line costs nothing and does not rot when a path moves.
apps/desktop/src-tauri/resources/node_modules/
# Card L4: staged by the same script's stageNotice() from the committed root
# NOTICE (scripts/generate-notice.mjs), so Vite's default public/ passthrough
# carries it into dist/NOTICE → the webview bundle. The root NOTICE is the
# tracked source of truth; this copy is emitted, not authored.
apps/desktop/public/NOTICE

# Operational dry-run tool: a self-contained bundle emitted by
# `pnpm --filter @flowmic/server-core build:tools` from the tracked source at
# apps/server-core/src/tools/provenance-dryrun.ts. Emitted, not authored — and it
# MUST be rebuilt rather than fetched from git, because a stale copy would report
# on whichever settings/provenance.ts it was built from instead of the one about
# to ship.
scripts/provenance-dryrun.mjs

# release artifacts
release/
publish/
# The mac half of a release, staged here after it is built on the Mac. Same
# category as publish/, and it was NOT ignored: 124MB of zips sat untracked and
# blew the gate receipt's dirty-tree budget every run (scripts/gate-receipt.mjs
# MAX_DIRTY_BYTES), so every publish re-ran the full gate instead of reusing a
# proof. Stricter, not looser — but the cause was an ignore rule that never
# followed the mac artefacts across.
publish-mac/

# Log from the UI-automation harness used for on-device runs (r8-pc.py). Output
# of a tool, not of the product.
@AutomationLog.txt

# env / secrets — never commit
.env
.env.*
*.jks
*.keystore
key.properties
vps.env

# local scratch (gitignored by convention, see CLAUDE.md)
.local/

# editor / os
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/settings.json

# logs
*.log
window-forensics.log

.playwright-mcp/

# worker 临时输出（0.2.25 实战：git add -A 把它们扫进过仓库一次）
.tmp-*

# Python bytecode cache. Same reason as the line above, and it is not
# hypothetical: the moment a `.py` under scripts/ was first RUN in this repo
# (C11's OPS-4 drills, 2026-08-12), `scripts/__pycache__/` appeared untracked and
# was one `git add -A` away from being committed. The three older tracked `.py`
# files are brand build scripts that nobody runs from here, which is the only
# reason this never came up before.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
